								text: "<p>Having utterly spurned corruptible things and thoughts * which draw one down to the depths, O venerable martyr Dometius, * thou didst show thyself to be a great leader of monks, * turning to fear the wrath of the king who did not wish to worship Christ as the true God. * Wherefore, thou didst repose, chanting the hymn; ** God is with me, and no one is against me!</p>",
